core(3,[
('high-temperature disorder and onset of superionic conductivity','produce little further reduction in','lattice thermal conductivity','Little reduction in lattice thermal conductivity was observed in the high-temperature phase, despite the increased disorder on the cation site and the onset of superionic conductivity.','observed_limited_effect'),
('anharmonic bonding and diffuson dominated transport','suggested joint origin of','inherently low lattice thermal conductivity in ACrX2','This suggests that the low lattice thermal conductivity in ACrX2 compounds is an inherent property of the crystal structure, caused by anharmonic bonding and diffuson dominated transport.','suggested_joint')],reason='聚焦本研究热输运结论，不把引言泛化机制再计为独立核心关系。')
core(4,[
('ionic bonding character and large Born effective charges','jointly cause','colossal phonon-electric field coupling','It is driven by the colossal phonon-electric field coupling arising from the domination of ionic character in the interatomic bonds and Born effective or dynamical charges as high as 7.4e on the Hf ions, which is seven times that on Mo in MoS2 single layer.','computational_joint'),
('colossal phonon-electric field coupling','drives','large LO-TO splitting','It is driven by the colossal phonon-electric field coupling','computational_prediction'),
('including non-analytic correction','increases calculated','lattice thermal conductivity','Enhancement in k(L) occurs in HfS2 (2.19 to 4.1 W m(-1) K-1), HfSe2 (1.23 to 1.7 W m(-1) K-1) and HfSSe (1.78 to 2.2 W m(-1) K-1) upon the incorporation of the non-analytic correction term.','computational_prediction'),
('large mass, low velocities, Debye temperature, stiffness, lifetimes, heat capacity and strong anharmonicity','collectively explain','low lattice thermal conductivity','Large atomic mass of Hf (178.5 u), small phonon group velocities (4-5 km s(-1)), low Debye temperature (similar to 166 K), low bond and elastic stiffness (Young\'s modulus similar to 75 N m(-1)), small phonon lifetimes (similar to 6 ps), low specific heat capacity (similar to 17 J K-1 mol(-1)) and strong anharmonicity are collectively found to be the factors responsible for such a low k(L).','computational_joint')])
